Got this working on opencode 1.14.22. Three separate problems stacking on top of each other:

1. **AgentRouter fingerprints the HTTP client**. Their backend is OneAPI-based (you can see `X-Oneapi-Request-Id` in response headers), and unless the request looks like Claude Code they reject it with `unauthorized client detected`. A spoofed `User-Agent` alone isn't enough, you also need the `x-stainless-*` set and `anthropic-*` headers that the real Claude Code CLI sends.

2. **opencode bug [#22608](https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/issues/22608)**: custom `headers` in [opencode.json](cci:7://file:///c:/Users/prism/.config/opencode/opencode.json:0:0-0:0) (especially `User-Agent`) are silently dropped before fetch. So any config-based approach (like the RooCode one posted above) can't work regardless of what you put in there.

3. **AgentRouter emits a malformed `data: null` SSE chunk** inside streams, which makes the AI SDK's Zod validator throw `Type validation failed: Value: null` has to be filtered.

Workaround: a small plugin that patches [globalThis.fetch](cci:1://file:///c:/Users/prism/.config/opencode/plugins/agentrouter-headers.js:68:2-96:4) for `agentrouter.org` only while other providers are untouched.

### `~/.config/opencode/opencode.json`

```json
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "provider": {
    "agentrouter": {
      "npm": "@ai-sdk/openai-compatible",
      "name": "agentrouter",
      "options": {
        "baseURL": "https://agentrouter.org/v1",
        "apiKey": "sk-YOUR_KEY"
      },
      "models": {
        "glm-4.6":                   { "name": "glm-4.6",                   "limit": { "context": 200000, "output": 65536 } },
        "claude-opus-4-6":           { "name": "claude-opus-4-6",           "limit": { "context": 200000, "output": 65536 } },
        "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001": { "name": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "limit": { "context": 200000, "output": 65536 } },
        "deepseek-v3.1":             { "name": "deepseek-v3.1",             "limit": { "context": 200000, "output": 65536 } }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

No `headers` block, the plugin does that. `apiKey` handles `Authorization: Bearer` automatically via the SDK.
> Notice: I may be wrong with the upstream limits. Needs to be checked.

### `~/.config/opencode/plugins/agentrouter-headers.js`

```js
// Scoped strictly to agentrouter.org. Other providers unaffected.
const AGENTROUTER_HOST = "agentrouter.org";

const INJECTED_HEADERS = {
  "User-Agent": "claude-cli/1.0.108 (external, cli)",
  "anthropic-version": "2023-06-01",
  "anthropic-beta": "claude-code-20250219,oauth-2025-04-20",
  "anthropic-dangerous-direct-browser-access": "true",
  "x-app": "cli",
  "x-stainless-lang": "js",
  "x-stainless-package-version": "0.55.1",
  "x-stainless-os": "Windows",
  "x-stainless-arch": "x64",
  "x-stainless-runtime": "node",
  "x-stainless-runtime-version": "v22.0.0",
};

function isAgentRouterUrl(url) {
  try {
    const p = typeof url === "string" ? new URL(url) : new URL(url.url ?? url.href ?? String(url));
    return p.hostname.endsWith(AGENTROUTER_HOST);
  } catch { return false; }
}

